### Billing V1 ledger payment — implemented, opt-in, NOT live by default
### Requires MEDIFLOW_BILLING_LEDGER_ENABLED=true and an existing authoritative V4 payment
### request, V5 exact target row and matching charges. This file does not create or seed them.
### Replace paymentRequestId with an actual request ID. Use a signed ADMIN/CASHIER access token.
### New V1 receipts/grants stay DB-held by V6 even when the API is enabled. Legacy invoice pay
### endpoints are unchanged. INSURANCE is not a cash receipt method on this new endpoint.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@billingServiceHost = http://localhost:8086
@paymentRequestId = replace-with-authoritative-payment-request-uuid
# @token = paste-access-token-here
# @serviceToken = signed SYSTEM token for clinical-service or lab-service

### Record an installment (200); retry with the SAME key and business fields for safe replay.
### Change the key only for another real installment. Amount must not exceed the remainder.
### Wrong actor/key reuse -> 409; expired/closed/wrong target/currency -> 422; absent request -> 404.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/billing/payment-requests/{{paymentRequestId}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-ID: 9e6c524e-a2e0-4ca9-ac20-6c61f93ae091

{
  "idempotencyKey": "replace-with-real-cashier-operation-key",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "VND",
  "paymentMethod": "CASH",
  "providerReference": null
}

### Implemented cashier-recorded refund (201), OFF unless BOTH ledger + refunds flags are true.
### Gateway routing is not changed by this slice; verify its owner policy before calling via @host.
### Completed CASH/TRANSFER recording only; no bank/provider instruction is issued.
### Original payment/allocations are immutable; the refund appends linked reversal allocations.
### Same key/actor/reason/method/amount replays. Settled/closed account requires explicit reopen policy.
@originalTransactionId = replace-with-real-completed-payment-uuid
POST {{host}}/api/v1/billing/transactions/{{originalTransactionId}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-ID: 9e6c524e-a2e0-4ca9-ac20-6c61f93ae091

{
  "idempotencyKey": "replace-with-real-cashier-refund-key",
  "amount": 20.00,
  "reason": "Approved cashier refund; internal audit only",
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}
### Rx terminal adjustment: ADMIN/CASHIER, opt-in ledger + Rx issuer; not a completed refund
### Gateway policy is unchanged; this route needs its owner's routing acceptance before gateway use.
@prescriptionId = replace-with-authoritative-prescription-uuid
GET {{host}}/api/v1/billing/prescription-adjustments/{{prescriptionId}}/refunds-due
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Correlation-Id: rx-adjustment-read

### Read-only admission reconciliation: ADMIN/CASHIER signed access token, NOT a settlement.
### Requires ledger + MEDIFLOW_BILLING_SETTLEMENT_PREVIEW_ENABLED=true. Flags default false.
### Manual developer diagnostic directly against Billing; no new Gateway route is approved here.
### Report must not call this endpoint. No payment, approval, allocation or outbox is written.
### snapshotOnly=true / finalSettlement=false even when estimatedOutcome=PAID_IN_FULL.
@billingDiagnosticHost = http://localhost:8086
@accountId = replace-with-authoritative-admission-billing-account-uuid
GET {{billingDiagnosticHost}}/api/v1/billing/accounts/{{accountId}}/settlement-preview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Correlation-Id: admission-settlement-preview

### Non-final immutable reconciliation: ADMIN/CASHIER, signed UUID access token.
### Requires ledger + settlement-preview + MEDIFLOW_BILLING_RECONCILIATION_ENABLED=true (all off by default).
### Manual Billing diagnostic; Gateway policy/route acceptance is not changed here.
### Persisted ledger amounts only: no caller money/approval input. Held event is settlement.reconciled, NOT settlement.completed.
### Retry SAME key on 503; a different successful key creates another account-local reconciliation revision.
POST {{billingDiagnosticHost}}/api/v1/billing/accounts/{{accountId}}/settlement-reconciliations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: replace-with-unique-cashier-reconciliation-key

### Admit an exact EXAM or LAB_TEST execution (200); SYSTEM service identity only.
### clinical-service may start EXAM; lab-service may start LAB_TEST. Use the target UUID as both
### operationId and sourceId so local transaction retries use the same one-time receipt. A replay
### rechecks current Billing eligibility and returns 409 after cancellation/refund revokes the grant.
@financialClearanceId = replace-with-current-clearance-uuid
@executionSourceId = replace-with-exact-exam-or-lab-test-uuid
@patientId = replace-with-clearance-patient-uuid
@careEpisodeId = replace-with-clearance-episode-uuid
POST {{billingServiceHost}}/api/v1/billing/financial-clearances/{{financialClearanceId}}/execution-starts
Authorization: Bearer {{serviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: 9e6c524e-a2e0-4ca9-ac20-6c61f93ae092

{
  "operationId": "{{executionSourceId}}",
  "sourceType": "LAB_TEST",
  "sourceId": "{{executionSourceId}}",
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
  "careEpisodeType": "OUTPATIENT_VISIT",
  "careEpisodeId": "{{careEpisodeId}}"
}

### Read the cancellation adjustment for one exact LAB_TEST (ADMIN/CASHIER access token).
### EXAM uses /exam-adjustments/{appointmentId}/refunds-due. This is a read-only due view;
### every outpatient refund still requires accepted cancellation and is capped by remaining due.
GET {{billingServiceHost}}/api/v1/billing/lab-adjustments/{{executionSourceId}}/refunds-due
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Correlation-Id: lab-adjustment-read

### Read the cancellation adjustment for one exact EXAM appointment.
GET {{billingServiceHost}}/api/v1/billing/exam-adjustments/{{executionSourceId}}/refunds-due
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Correlation-Id: exam-adjustment-read
